{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>I knew you</b> [in a land of] <b>Ta'aluvot</b> [drought]: a land of wilderness and thirst, and so too in the Ishmaelite language. And its being read as <i>ta'alot</i> [palanquin/litters] is by way of derash and not by way of peshat."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {0 "The comment addresses the word תלאובות (Hosea 13:5); Ibn Ezra notes an alternative reading tradition that repoints it as תלאות, which he classifies as derash rather than peshat."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:51:07.067939792Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}